From e74a6cf6082ec7bf0ac36268d29bf2b782554240 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naster17 <naster17.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:42:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] rpc : async cross-backend copies + async-path wire
 compression (GGML_RPC_ASYNC_COPY)

Implement cpy_tensor_async: host<->RPC via queued set/get; cross-server via GET->SET
chained with a wait_before future (queue position preserves order; single-threaded
submission keeps it acyclic). BF16/Q8_0 compression added to set_tensor_async;
cross-server copies use BF16 wire when eligible. No protocol change.
Verified: test-rpc-multi-server OK; greedy output identical on 2-board LFM3 RPC.
Perf on 1GbE 2xBC-250: NEUTRAL (gemma4 pp2048 1085->1081, tg 83.3->83.0) - the
cluster is wire/RTT-bound, not copy-sync-bound. Kept env-gated for faster links.

Assisted-by: Qwen3.8-Max
